#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Combine every broker's positions from Redis into one positions document, the way the REST API's
`/api/portfolio/positions` answers, and write it to the Redis key `unified:portfolio:positions` every half second.

    bin/unified/portfolio/positions
    redis-cli GET unified:portfolio:positions

Nothing here calls a broker. Each broker's open positions are already kept in Redis, merged from its REST positions and,
for Fyers, Groww, Kotak and Wisdom Capital, its position update stream, as the hash `<broker>:portfolio:positions`: one
field per position, each value `{"observed_at", "source", "position", "data"}`. The instruments are kept by
`bin/unified/instruments/map` and live prices by `bin/unified/instruments/websocket_quotes` in `unified:quotes:live`, so this reads those and
interprets them.

**The document** has the REST API's shape:

    {"net": [...], "day": [...], "summary": {"net": {...}, "day": {...}}, "brokers": [...], "as_of": ...}

`net` is every position open now, carried or taken today; `day` is today's activity alone, which only Zerodha and Wisdom
Capital report - their hash fields start `DAY:` or `NET:` - so `day` holds only theirs. Stoxkart's fields would start `DAY:`
too if Stoxkart ever sent a day view, which it has not. A position is `instrument_id`,
`symbol`, `exchange`, `segment`, `expiry_date`, `strike_price`, `option_type`, `product` (`delivery`, `intraday`,
`carry`, `margin_trading`, `cover`, `bracket`), `quantity` (signed), `buy` and `sell` (`quantity`, `average_price`,
`value`), `average_price`, `last_price`, `pnl` (`realized`, `unrealized`, `total`), `day_change` and
`day_change_percentage`, sorted by symbol, expiry, strike, option type and product. Each summary is `count`,
`realized_pnl`, `unrealized_pnl` and `total_pnl`.

**Each broker's position** is read from the entry's
`data`, the broker's own row. Two brokers' update streams send a different shape from their REST positions, so a
websocket entry from Fyers or Groww is read from its normalized `position` instead:

| broker | token, venue | quantity | bought, sold | profit, prices |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| zerodha | `instrument_token`, `exchange` | `quantity` | `buy_quantity`/`buy_value`, `sell_quantity`/`sell_value` | `realised`, `unrealised`, `last_price`, `close_price` |
| dhan | `securityId`, `exchangeSegment` | `netQty` | `buyQty` at `buyAvg`, `sellQty` at `sellAvg` | `realizedProfit`, `unrealizedProfit` |
| flattrade, shoonya | `token`, `exch` | `netqty` | today's and carried legs added | `rpnl`, `urmtom`, `lp`, `c` |
| fyers (REST) | `fyToken`, symbol prefix and `segment` | `netQty` | `buyQty`/`buyVal`, `sellQty`/`sellVal` | `realized_profit`, `unrealized_profit`, `ltp` |
| fyers (stream) | `instrument_token`, `exchange` and `segment` | `quantity` | `buy_*`, `sell_*` values | `realized_pnl`, `unrealized_pnl` |
| groww (REST) | no token, `exchange` and `segment` | `quantity` | `credit_quantity` at `credit_price`, `debit_quantity` at `debit_price` | none |
| groww (stream) | no token, `exchange`, derivatives | `quantity` | the NSE and BSE legs, added | none |
| indmoney | `security_id`, `exchange` or `segment` | `net_qty` | `buy_qty`/`buy_value`, `sell_qty`/`sell_value` | `realized_pnl`, `unrealized_pnl`, `last_price` |
| kotak | `tok`, `exSeg` | today's and carried buys less sells | `flBuyQty` + `cfBuyQty` at `buyAmt` + `cfBuyAmt`, and sells | none |
| stoxkart | `token`, `exchange` | `net_quantity` | `buy_quantity`/`buy_value`, `sell_quantity`/`sell_value` | `mark_to_market` as unrealized, `last_trade_price` |
| wisdom_capital | `ExchangeInstrumentID`, `ExchangeSegment` | `Quantity` | `OpenBuyQuantity`/`BuyAmount`, `OpenSellQuantity`/`SellAmount` | `RealizedMTM`, `UnrealizedMTM` |

**Resolving, merging and pricing.** A token is looked up in `unified:broker_tokens` only among the
segments its venue's kind trades on that exchange - cash, equity/index/fixed income derivatives, currency or commodity -
and several survivors are taken in vocabulary order, then by symbol and id; a Groww cash position, with no token, is
looked up by symbol in `unified:instrument_symbols`. Positions are one row when they share an instrument and a product,
or, unresolved, an exchange, a symbol and a product; quantities, values and profits add up, and averages come from the
sums. A resolved row's last price comes from its instrument's quote in `unified:quotes:live`, with the quote's
`previous_close` as the previous close, falling back to the price and previous close a broker sent when
there is no quote. Profit stays the brokers' own.

**Brokers.** `brokers` says, for each broker, how its hash was read, with `as_of` the newer of the newest entry's
`observed_at` and the last successful poll, which `bin/<broker>/portfolio/positions` records in
`<broker>:portfolio:positions:polled_at`: `ok`; `stale` when that is more than a minute ago - the poller refreshes every
entry and records itself on every poll, so its scripts may have stopped, and its positions are still included; `missing`
when there is neither a hash nor a recorded poll, so the broker's scripts have not run today - a flat account being read
is `ok` with no positions; or `unreadable` when no entry could be decoded.

Written with SET every half second. Runs until Ctrl+C or SIGTERM; a Redis that cannot be reached is logged and tried
again. Reads only - it places no orders.
"""

